IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P7-gates: the two gates this part calls and the seam it takes from Article 2(2).
-- Articles 57 to 63 and 71 are in the keel's provision group `General`; Articles 64 to 70 are in the group
-- `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` (Art 113 as amended, third paragraph (b)).
-- The two wrappers only pass the group and the core's constants to the keel's applicability function
-- `Art 113 the provision group applies`; they state no date. A question that is not about one AI system passes
-- `the route to pass when no AI system is in question`, `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` and FALSE.
-- The seam S14 (Article 2(2)): a function that Article 2(2) can cut off asks `Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply`, which calls
-- the keel's `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` for the Article of the provision.

§ `Article 113: the group General (Articles 57 to 63 and 71)`

-- src:1657 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
@ref Art 113 second paragraph (the general date of application) (src:1657)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

§ `Article 113 point (b): the group of Chapter VII (Articles 64 to 70)`

-- src:1662 | (b) Chapter III Section 4, Chapter V, Chapter VII and Chapter XII and Article 78 shall apply from 2 August 2025, with the exception of Article 101;
@ref Art 113(b) (Chapter VII from 2 August 2025) (src:1662)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

§ `Seam S14: what Article 2(2) does to the provision (a call to the keel)`

-- The keel's `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` answers
-- JUST FALSE (the provision does not apply: "only ... shall apply"), JUST TRUE (it applies) or NOTHING (Article 2(2) does not speak to the system).
-- A function that Article 2(2) can cut off asks this gate first: where the keel answers JUST FALSE the part answers JUST FALSE; where it answers NOTHING or JUST TRUE
-- the part answers on its own provision. The Article reference of the provision is its number, its letter ("a" for Article 60a) and its paragraph.

-- The text is Article 2(2) (consolidated line 41), quoted with its `@ref` in the keel's `aia-scope`; this gate quotes nothing of its own, because line 41 is outside the range of this part.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the Article of the provision` IS A NUMBER
      `the letter of the Article of the provision` IS A STRING
      `the paragraph of the provision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 57 Article 2(2) leaves the provision to apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` (`Article reference` WITH number IS `the number of the Article of the provision`, letter IS `the letter of the Article of the provision`, paragraph IS `the paragraph of the provision`)
    WHEN JUST `the answer` THEN `the answer`
    OTHERWISE TRUE
